1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,880
I ran out of gas on a
state highway in Nevada a

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:05,140
little after ten at
night, about forty miles

3
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:05,940
from the nearest town.

4
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:07,600
That part was my fault.

5
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:11,860
I was twenty-two, driving from Reno to see
my sister in Arizona, and I'd skipped the

6
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:14,000
last station because the
prices were ridiculous

7
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,820
and I was sure there'd
be another one soon.

8
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:17,100
There wasn't.

9
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:21,200
The car started sputtering
on a long straight stretch

10
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,520
with nothing on either side but sagebrush

11
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:24,340
and dark hills.

12
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:27,560
I coasted onto the shoulder
and sat there with

13
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:29,760
my hazards on, listening to the engine

14
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:30,860
tick as it cooled.

15
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:33,160
I had one bar of signal.

16
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,200
I called roadside
assistance, gave them the

17
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:38,580
mile marker from my map app, and the woman

18
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,320
on the phone told me a tow truck would
be there in about ninety minutes.

19
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:43,540
She asked if I felt safe.

20
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:46,920
I said, yes, because what
else are you supposed to say?

21
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:50,480
The first thing I noticed
was how quiet it was.

22
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:53,820
When the engine stopped
ticking, there was nothing.

23
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:57,240
No wind, no insects, no traffic.

24
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:59,160
I could hear my own breathing.

25
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:02,020
Every few minutes, I'd
turn the key just far

26
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:03,520
enough to check the time on the dashboard,

27
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:05,620
then turned it off again
to save the battery.

28
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:10,920
I had half a bottle of water and a bag of
sunflower seeds, and I remember rationing

29
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:14,100
the water like I was in a survival
movie, which is funny now.

30
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,700
Around eleven, I saw a
light out in the desert.

31
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:20,480
It was far off to the
right, maybe a mile or

32
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,620
two, low to the ground, like a flashlight

33
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:23,800
or a lantern.

34
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:25,980
It didn't move for a long time.

35
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:30,020
Then it went out, and a few seconds
later it came back on, closer.

36
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:34,280
I told myself it was a ranch house, or
a radio tower, something on a timer.

37
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:37,260
I stopped looking at it
after that, because every

38
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:39,560
time I looked, it seemed a little nearer,

39
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:41,380
and I didn't like the
way that made me feel.

40
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:45,380
About thirty minutes in,
headlights came up behind me.

41
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:48,720
My stomach dropped, but then I
saw the light bar on the roof.

42
00:01:48,980 --> 00:01:50,180
It was a sheriff's deputy.

43
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:53,100
He pulled in behind me and
walked up with a flashlight,

44
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:55,440
an older guy with a gray mustache

45
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:56,900
and a tired, friendly face.

46
00:01:57,580 --> 00:01:58,460
I explained what happened.

47
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:00,700
He shook his head and
laughed a little, not

48
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:02,860
in a mean way, and said I wasn't the first

49
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,160
and wouldn't be the last.

50
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:07,940
He went back to his car and came
back with two bottles of water.

51
00:02:08,340 --> 00:02:11,600
Then he leaned down to my window,
and his voice changed a little.

52
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:15,580
He said, listen, keep your doors
locked until the tow gets here.

53
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:18,120
If anybody walks up to
the car, you don't roll

54
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:20,440
the window down, you call 911, and you

55
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:21,720
tell them Deputy Harlan is out here.

56
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:25,060
I asked him if something
had happened out here.

57
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:28,060
He looked down the road for
a second, then back at me.

58
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:31,860
He said, people walk this
road at night sometimes.

59
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:33,660
I don't stop for them anymore.

60
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:38,060
Then he told me to have a good night,
got back in his cruiser, and pulled away.

61
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,760
I watched his taillights
for a long time, until

62
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:44,120
they turned into one red dot, and then

63
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:44,920
nothing.

64
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:47,360
I called my sister to tell
her what was going on.

65
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,880
The call dropped twice
before it connected, and

66
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:51,400
when it did, the line was full of static,

67
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:52,780
like she was standing in wind.

68
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:55,820
I told her I'd run out of gas
and that a deputy had stopped.

69
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:58,780
She asked if I was okay, and I said yes.

70
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:01,100
Then she asked who was with me.

71
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:02,400
I said nobody.

72
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:05,120
She was quiet for a
second, and then she said

73
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:07,480
she could have sworn she heard someone in

74
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:09,980
The call dropped again,
and I couldn't get it back.

75
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:13,700
After that, the quiet felt different.

76
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:16,860
I locked the doors and checked them twice.

77
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:20,380
I sat with my phone in my lap and
kept looking in the side mirrors.

78
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:23,680
The road behind me was a straight
black line under the stars.

79
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:27,940
I could see maybe a quarter mile back,
and then it disappeared into the dark.

80
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:31,240
I told myself the deputy
was just being careful,

81
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:32,920
and he probably said that to everyone.

82
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:36,440
I tried playing a podcast,
but I turned it off

83
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:38,320
after a minute because I didn't like not

84
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:39,120
being able to hear.

85
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:42,660
At some point, I heard
gravel crunch somewhere

86
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:45,900
behind the car, just
once, the way it sounds

87
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:47,020
when someone shifts their weight.

88
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,900
I turned on my headlights and stared
into the mirrors until my eyes watered.

89
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:52,520
There was nothing back there.

90
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:56,520
I told myself it was an animal,
a coyote or a jackrabbit,

91
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:58,700
but I noticed I'd stopped breathing

92
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:01,360
while I listened, and I had to
remind myself to start again.

93
00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:05,520
The tow truck showed up about
an hour after the deputy left.

94
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:08,000
I almost cried when I
saw the amber lights.

95
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:12,240
The driver backed up in front of my
car, got out, and gave me a wave.

96
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:16,120
He was a big guy in a reflective
vest, probably in his fifties.

97
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:17,400
His name was Manny.

98
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:20,120
He told me to stay in the
car while he hooked it up.

99
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:21,240
It would only take a few minutes.

100
00:04:21,740 --> 00:04:23,120
I nodded and stayed put.

101
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:26,540
I was watching him in
my headlights, crouched

102
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:28,760
down at the front of my car, working with

103
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:29,560
the chains.

104
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:32,340
And then I looked in my rearview mirror.

105
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,780
There was a woman standing behind my car.

106
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:38,120
She wasn't on the road.

107
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:41,840
She was on the shoulder,
maybe ten feet back, at

108
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:43,880
the edge of the red glow
from my tail lights.

109
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:50,380
She was older, maybe sixties, thin, with
long gray hair and a hiking backpack.

110
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:53,500
She wasn't wearing a coat,
and it was cold enough

111
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:55,040
that I had the heat on until the battery

112
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:55,840
scared me.

113
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:57,800
I hadn't seen any headlights.

114
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:59,940
I hadn't heard footsteps on the gravel.

115
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:02,040
She was just there.

116
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,880
She didn't look lost or scared.

117
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,700
She didn't look like someone
whose car had broken down.

118
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:09,220
Her clothes were clean.

119
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:11,200
Her hair wasn't moving in the wind.

120
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:14,240
She stood there with
her hands at her sides,

121
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:17,240
completely still, the way people stand in

122
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:19,540
an elevator waiting for the doors to open.

123
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:21,300
I didn't move.

124
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:22,960
I watched her in the mirror.

125
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:25,960
She walked up along the
passenger side of the

126
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:28,380
car, slowly, and stopped at the back door.

127
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:31,980
Then she reached out
and pulled the handle.

128
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:33,880
It was locked.

129
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:37,460
She pulled it again, harder, and
the whole car rocked a little.

130
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:40,180
Then she bent down and looked
through the back window.

131
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,020
She wasn't looking at me.

132
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:45,780
She was looking at the back seat, like
she expected someone to be sitting there.

133
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:48,860
That was the part that
stuck with me later.

134
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:51,940
She wasn't checking whether
anyone was in the front.

135
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:54,400
She didn't care that I
was sitting right there.

136
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:58,220
She was looking at the
empty back seat with this

137
00:05:58,220 --> 00:06:00,800
patient, almost hopeful expression, like

138
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:04,740
she was waiting for someone she knew
to sit up and unlock the door for her.

139
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:06,460
I hit the horn.

140
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,040
I don't know why.

141
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:10,000
It was the only thing I could think of.

142
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,120
Manny stood up in front of the car.

143
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:15,180
The woman straightened up
and walked to my window,

144
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:17,300
the passenger side, and knocked on

145
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:19,600
the glass with one knuckle, very politely.

146
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:22,360
She leaned down and said,

147
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:23,600
My car's just up the road.

148
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:24,660
I've got a flat.

149
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:26,240
I just need a ride to it.

150
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:28,360
Her voice was normal.

151
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:30,420
That's what I keep coming back to.

152
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:33,220
It was a completely normal voice.

153
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,800
A little hoarse, like
somebody's grandmother.

154
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:37,600
I shook my head.

155
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:39,640
She smiled at me and said,

156
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:44,100
It's right up there and pointed down the
highway, in the direction I'd been driving.

157
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:47,940
Manny was walking around the
front of my car now, saying,

158
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:49,200
Hey, hey, ma'am.

159
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,560
I looked at him for maybe a second.

160
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,260
When I looked back at the
window, she wasn't there.

161
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,920
I turned all the way around in my seat.

162
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:58,240
The shoulder was empty.

163
00:06:58,500 --> 00:06:59,300
The road was empty.

164
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:02,220
Manny walked all the way around
my car with his flashlight.

165
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:05,000
He walked back along the
shoulder, maybe 50 yards.

166
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:07,120
There was nothing out there.

167
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:08,820
No footprints that we could see.

168
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:09,860
No sound.

169
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:10,880
Nothing.

170
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:12,500
The desert was flat for miles.

171
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:14,500
There wasn't anywhere for a person to go.

172
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:17,280
When he came back, he was breathing hard.

173
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:20,180
And he kept his flashlight pointed
at the ground near his boots,

174
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:22,480
like he didn't want to
see anything else with it.

175
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:24,720
He asked me if she'd touched the car.

176
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:27,120
I told him she'd pulled on the back door.

177
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:30,760
He walked around to that side and
looked at the handle for a long time,

178
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:31,960
without touching it.

179
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:35,540
He came back to my window
and asked if I was okay.

180
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,420
I told him what she'd said,

181
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:39,920
that her car was just up
the road with a flat.

182
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:42,340
He didn't say anything for a second.

183
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:45,180
Then he asked me to ride
up in the truck with him.

184
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:47,660
And he didn't really make
it sound like a question.

185
00:07:49,020 --> 00:07:51,360
We drove for about 20 minutes
before either of us talked.

186
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:53,320
We passed the place where she'd pointed.

187
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:55,540
We passed the next five miles after that.

188
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:57,740
There was no car on the side of that road.

189
00:07:58,100 --> 00:07:58,900
There was nothing.

190
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:01,000
Finally, Manny said,

191
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,700
She tell you it was a flat?

192
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:04,160
I said yes.

193
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:06,460
He nodded and kept his eyes on the road.

194
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:07,700
He said,

195
00:08:07,660 --> 00:08:09,880
You're the third one this
year, she's told that too.

196
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:11,580
The other two opened the door.

197
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:13,740
I asked him what happened to them.

198
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,160
He didn't answer me.

199
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:16,480
He just turned the radio on.

